<title>UK: BNP sets $150 million step-up perpetual FRN.</title>
<headline>BNP sets $150 million step-up perpetual FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager CS First Boston.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANQUE NATIONALE DE PARIS</p>
<p> AMT    $150 MLN	BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY  * PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN  ** 62.5 BP   PAY DATE    06.NOV.96</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A1	  ISS PRICE  99.59     FULL FEES   0.625</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A-	  REOFFER    99.59</p>
<p> NOTES    * CALL AT PAR FROM NOVEMBER 2006</p>
<p>	   ** TO NOVEMBER 2006, 2.125 PERCENT THEREAFTER</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/FR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  0.50	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
